ther \\(m+1\\) points of the outer layer.\n   * \\(L_{2}\\) contains the remaining points of the outer layer, again \\(m+1\\)\n     points.\n\n   None of the outer‑layer points lies on any line of \\(\\mathcal L_{2m-1}\\) because\n   every line of \\(\\mathcal L_{2m-1}\\) is contained in the smaller triangle\n   \\(T_{2m-1}\\).  Consequently  \n\n   \\[\n   \\mathcal L_{2m+1}= \\mathcal L_{2m-1}\\cup\\{L_{1},L_{2}\\}\n   \\]\n\n   is a family of \\(2m+1\\) sunny lines covering all of \\(T_{2m+1}\\).  ∎\n\n   Lemma 2 therefore supplies a covering for every odd \\(k\\).\n\n4. **Completion of the original problem.**  \n\n   *If \\(k=0\\).*  Take the \\(n\\) vertical lines \\(x=1,\\dots ,x=n\\); all are\n   non‑sunny and every required point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) has\n   \\(a\\le n\\), hence lies on one of them.\n\n   *If \\(k\\) is odd and \\(1\\le k\\le n\\).*  \n   Use the construction of Lemma 2 to cover the triangle \\(T_k\\) with exactly\n   \\(k\\) sunny lines.  The remaining points have abscissa at most \\(n-k\\); they\n   are covered by the vertical lines \\(x=1,\\dots ,x=n-k\\).  Altogether we have\n   \\(k+(n-k)=n\\) distinct lines, exactly \\(k\\) of which are sunny, and every\n   lattice point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) lies on at least one of them.\n\n   *If \\(k\\) is even and \\(k\\ge2\\).*  \n   By Lemma 1 the triangle \\(T_k\\) cannot be covered by \\(k\\) sunny lines, so\n   no configuration satisfying the statement exists.\n\n   Hence the admissible values of \\(k\\) are precisely those described in the\n   verdict.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k=0\\ \\text{or}\\ k\\ \\text{odd with}\\ 1\\le k\\le n\\;}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
